  ],
  "text" : "Context engineering is just giving your agent a map.\nHumans search when they know what they're looking for,\nbut we turn to agents\nwhen we're not really sure what we need,\nso they end up exploring more.\nThe obvious fix is to stuff everything\ninto the context window, but that'll backfire.\nThe model isn't really fine what you're looking for.\nThis is known as context rot.\nHaving one giant agents MD file does not work.\nWhen everything is important,\nnothing is, it can't cut through the noise\nto find what really matters.\nBut by creating a simple map,\na map in Markdown or an index in a database,\nYou hold pointers to files.\nYou concisely let the agent navigate where it needs to go.\nThe agent reads the map and drills into only what it needs\nto, retrieving that part."
}
